[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127359,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Elastofibroma is a benign soft tissue tumour characterized by abnormal elastic fibres, bland fibroblasts, and myxoid stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127360,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8820/0 Elastofibroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127361,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FB51.Y &amp; XH3BQ8 Other specified fibroblastic disorders &amp; Elastofibroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127362,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> elastofibroma dorsi.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127363,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127364,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Elastofibroma is most often subscapular. It sometimes involves the chest wall but can occur anywhere.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127365,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are slow-growing, typically solitary, and usually asymptomatic, but they can cause pain, limitation of movement, or scapular snapping/impingement.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127366,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Elastofibroma most commonly affects elderly adults, with a female predominance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127367,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown. Some cases run in families {9696981}; in one series, one third of the patients reported a familial history {7116305}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127368,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Elastofibromas have a variety of chromosomal abnormalities. Copy gains (including gains of Xq) {12165800}, alterations to chromosome&nbsp;1, and t(8;12)(q22;q24.3) {11343783} and/or t(2;19) and (X;1) rearrangements {11458949} have been found in some of the cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127369,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Elastofibromas are poorly defined firm masses ranging in size from 50 to 100&nbsp;mm. The cut surface is variegated grey and white, with small areas of adipose tissue.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127370,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Elastofibromas are large and have poorly defined borders. They are often hypocellular with degenerative collagen fibres that are fragmented, thickened, and globular; these can be highlighted with Verhoeff elastic staining. Variable proportions of bland uniform small spindle cells, aggregates of mature adipocytes, and myxoid stroma are present {7116305}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127371,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are bland spindle cells, fragmented degenerative collagen fibres (braid-like and globular) and mature adipocytes {23554149}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127372,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127373,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> fragmented, thickened, and globular collagenous fibres; bland spindle cells; admixed mature adipocytes and myxoid stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127374,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127375,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 386,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Elastofibroma is benign, and simple excision is curative {7116305; 20130320}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]